// Molly's provenance unit test "repeat rule firings with different contributing tuples (missing fields are part of a
// join)" (R06 §12.6, ProvenanceSuite): c(loc, 1) is derived by two firings of one rule, one through M = x and one
// through M = y. Blossom golden corpus, transcribed from R06 (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

c(L, V) :- b(L, M, V), a(L, M, V);

a("loc", "x", 1)@1;
a("loc", "y", 1)@1;
b("loc", "x", 1)@1;
b("loc", "y", 1)@1;
